  "calculation_notes": [
    "Formation dates use conservative public-availability dates; the 2023 vintage uses the dated official J.P. Morgan public page because the archived release states only December 2022.",
    "Federal Reserve signals are arithmetic means of overlapping annual median revisions in real GDP growth, PCE inflation, and the federal funds rate.",
    "IMF signals use the mean revision for the two published world-growth years; unavailable inflation or policy-rate revisions are neutralized to zero and marked missing.",
    "The 2025-vintage IMF October 2024 WEO was published after the CMA formation date and is therefore excluded.",
    "South Korea revisions are neutralized where a consistent point-in-time official revision series was not reconstructed; no later observation is substituted."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "J.P. Morgan CMA values target a 10-to-15-year horizon and are not designed for one-year tactical forecasts.",
    "The available KIS adjusted-price history begins in 2020, so this file supports a 12-month calibration backtest only.",
    "Current classifications and the currently listed pension-eligible universe create classification and survivorship bias.",
    "Historical ETF fee vintages are unavailable, so the backtest compares gross planning assumptions with gross total returns and excludes costs."
  ]
